   \]

2. **Convert the volume flow rate to cm³/s**:  
   \[
   \text{Volume flow rate} = 10 \text{ cm}^3 \text{ min}^{-1} = \frac{10}{60} \text{ cm}^3 \text{ s}^{-1} = 0.167 \text{ cm}^3 \text{ s}^{-1}
   \]

3. **Calculate the linear flow rate (time per cm)**:  
   \[
   \text{Linear flow rate} = \frac{\text{Tube volume per cm}}{\text{Volume flow rate}} = \frac{7.8 \times 10^{-5} \text{ cm}^3}{0.167 \text{ cm}^3 \text{ s}^{-1}} = 4.7 \times 10^{-4} \text{ s cm}^{-1}
   \]

4. **Determine the reaction times**:  
