Consider a p-channel MOSFET with an oxide thickness of 500 Å and a donor doping concentration \(N_d = 10^{16} \text{ cm}^{-3}\). Calculate the body-to-source voltage (\(V_{BS}\)) needed to shift the threshold voltage (\(V_T\)) from its value at \(V_{BS} = 0\) by \(-1.0\) V.
</USER_REQUEST>

<GROUND_TRUTH>
To calculate the body-to-source voltage (\(V_{BS}\)) required to shift the threshold voltage (\(V_T\)) by \(-1.0\) V, we use the body effect formula for a p-channel MOSFET:

\[
\Delta V_T = \gamma \left( \sqrt{|2\phi_F + V_{BS}|} - \sqrt{|2\phi_F|} \right)
\]

